  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-ZAF103</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of constituents to create decent and productive employment in the rural economy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">South Africa faces the triple challenge of high unemployment, inequality, and poverty.  Government has placed a high priority on the development of a National Employment Policy (NEP) to address the challenges of both labour demand and labour supply to tackle the high levels of unemployment. Amidst the rising challenge of climate change the NEP is set to respond to the implications of a shift to a lower carbon economy on jobs and labour market. Government has underpinned the importance of infrastructure Development and labour-intensive investment programmes for inclusive growth and the Expanded Public Works Programme has been the entry point for the ILO&#x2019;s support to the roll-out of Government&#x2019;s infrastructure development programme through the application of labour-intensive methodologies. Government is to develop a policy for the EPWP and a fifth Phase that seeks to create 5 million work opportunities over the next 5 years ending March 2029. 
The strategy will focus on capacity support to a facilitated stakeholder engagement on the draft NEP, including with strategic Government clusters, Nedlac among others; technical assistance in the development of the NEP implementation plan; technical support for the application of labour-intensive and climate smart approaches and tools in the roll-out of Government&#x2019;s infrastructure development programme at local government level; policy and capacity support towards the development of a policy for the EPWP, and the 5th Phase EPWP</narrative>
  </description>
